From: NEMO Phase II executor <executor@nemo.local>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 18:07:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Phase II: coagulation reaction-generation infrastructure
 (default-off)

Rung 1 (pure grain coagulation) encoded as bilinear pseudo-reactions that
flow through the existing chemistry RHS/Jacobian, per the locked design:
one reaction per unordered bin pair (i,j), bin_i+bin_j -> eps*bin_k +
(1-eps)*bin_{k+1}; kernel (with the 1/2 self-pair factor) on reaction_rates,
Podolak/Brauer split on the per-product weight field, loss unweighted. Mass
is exact by construction (eps*m_k + (1-eps)*m_{k+1} = m_i+m_j).

New: src/dust/dustevolution.f90 (module dust_evolution)
  - coag_pair_target: single source of truth for pair -> (bins,weights);
    top-bin OVERFLOW (m_i+m_j > m_N) handled as Rung 1 policy (c) -- the
    reaction is simply not generated (mass-exact, keeps the analytic gate
    valid). Skipped pairs are a LOUD deferral: recorded at init, counted, and
    exposed via dust_coagulation_dropped_flux() (sum K_ij n_i n_j over skipped
    pairs) which must read ~0 over the validation window.
  - dust_coagulation_count / _inject_static / _set_rates: count before
    get_array_sizes; inject at the NAME level after read_reactions (resolved to
    IDs by set_chemical_reactants, so no INDGRAIN plumbing) before index_datas'
    type scan; set the constant kernel after init_reaction_rates.
  - guards: fatal error on an ice-bearing network (J/K species) since
    coagulation does not transport ice until Rung 2; fatal if COAGULATION_TYPE
    (50) collides with a chemistry type.

Wiring (all guarded by `coagulation`, default .false.):
  - global_variables: coagulation flag, constant_kernel_k0, kernel selector,
    reaction counters, skipped-pair store, COAGULATION_TYPE=50; get_array_sizes
    appends nb_coagulation_reactions (0 when off).
  - input_output: keyword-parser cases coagulation / coagulation_kernel /
    constant_kernel_k0 (absent keywords default safely).
  - gasgrain init_gasgrain: three guarded calls at the required points.
  - preliminary_tests: exempt COAGULATION_TYPE from element/charge integer
    balance (coag conserves mass via weights, validated by gate a, not here).
  - Makefile: dustevolution.f90 between ode_solver and gasgrain.

Verification: default build (-O2 and -O0) compiles+links clean; the full-init
jac_weight_check smoke test passes IDENTICALLY to the parent commit (13450
entries, worst reldiff 1.8006e-3, 0 weight bugs), proving the entire network
build + RHS + Jacobian are bit-unchanged with coagulation off. Combined with
the default-off guards (nothing new runs; nb_reactions unchanged) this
establishes byte-identity of the default path. The coagulation-ON path is NOT
yet validated -- that needs the dust-only fixture (next), together with the
mass-conservation gate (a) and the M0-decay analytic gate (b1).
